            <div xml:id="d311">

                <pb facs="0528" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg514"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">794A.00/9–1450: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in China
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-09-19T17:00:00-04:00">September 19,
                            1950—5 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>259. ReDeptel 214 Sept 4. Dept notes Ch’en Ch’eng at memorial service Sept 4 set
                    forth his “administration plan” for coming year, with plan divided into
                    pre-counter-offensive, general counter-offensive and post-counter-offensive
                    periods. Direction Nat thinking clear to see.</p>
                <p>US Govt’s position is not in support of any Nat program to return to mainland but
                    is aimed simply at protecting Formosa from attack. As you will appreciate
                    handling of matter in UNSC and UNGA in effort to achieve pacific settlement of
                    problems centering on island is delicate operation, with many complications
                    posed by reasons attitudes of powerful friends US and China, particularly UK and
                    India. Actions taken by Nat Govt prejudicial to pacific solution problem cld in
                    opinion US Govt hardly work otherwise than to detriment Nat Govt itself.</p>
                <p>Above for background in ur conversations with Nat officials.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
